  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#table-descriptions-techniques:the-details-element\n\n> details\n> I coded my table caption with the details as shown here but when it is rendered in the browser (tested in Firefox version 45.0.1and Google Chrome Version 49.0.2623.87), the browsers add a closing `</p>` to the end of the caption line above the `<details>` tag. Then a syntax checker says the closing `</p>` shouldn't be there. This happens with every table caption.  Why is it getting added?\n> See the attached files.\n> Example for caption with details:\n> ![example-of-caption-details](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/2455734/13987455/fe03bcc2-f0dd-11e5-834a-30dc3e2ea0a1.png)\n> My original code:\n> ![original-coding](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/2455734/13987485/29bff894-f0de-11e5-8477-604544967634.png)\n> How the code got rendered in the browsers:\n> ![syntax-checker-caption-error](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/2455734/13987503/3889fae6-f0de-11e5-8144-731e3e74ccb3.png)\n",
